# Build after code/spec changes

**Canonical:** [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) (Builds) · [`AGENT_READINESS.md`](../../docs/AGENT_READINESS.md) § Tiered validation.

## Default (maintainability / most edits)

- **Do not** run a full PyInstaller build on every source edit — it is slow and not required to validate logic.
- **Do** run **`run_tests.bat`** (T2) before claiming done on production changes.
- **Do** run **`build_ci.bat`** (or `build_and_deploy_v6.bat`) when the user asks for an exe, before field-test handoff, or when **`BSODAnalyzer.spec`** / packaging layout changes.

From project root:

```bat
set BUILD_NOPAUSE=1
call build_ci.bat
```

## When spec or entrypoint changes

Edits to **`BSODAnalyzer.spec`** or packaging-critical paths in **`bsod_analyzer.py`** → run **T2 tests**, then **build** in the same task if the deliverable is a portable exe.

Use `build_ci.bat` / `build_and_deploy_v6.bat` and `BSODAnalyzer_v6\` only.
